  "chapter": {
    "number": 134,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(135) Alleluia."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Praise you⌃ the name of the Lord; praise the Lord, you⌃ his servants,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Praise you⌃ the Lord; for the Lord is good: sing praises to his name; for it is good.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord has chosen Jacob for himself, and Israel for his peculiar treasure.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I know that the Lord is great, and our Lord is above all gods;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "all that the Lord willed, he did in heaven, and on the earth, in the sea, and in all deeps.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who brings up clouds from the extremity of the earth: he has made lightnings for the rain: he brings winds out of his treasures.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who struck the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and beast.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent signs and wonders into the midst of you, O Egypt, on Pharao, and on all his servants.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who struck many nations, and killed mighty kings;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Seon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Basan, and all the kingdoms of Chanaan:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and gave their land for an inheritance, an inheritance to Israel his people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, your name endures for ever, and your memorial to all generations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord shall judge his people, and comfort himself concerning his servants.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The idols of the heathen are silver and gold, the works of men's hands.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have a mouth, but they can’t speak; they have eyes, but they can’t see;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "they have ears, but they can’t hear; for there is no breath in their mouth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let those who make them be made like to them; and all those who trust in them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O house of Israel, bless you⌃ the Lord: O house of Aaron, bless you⌃ the Lord:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O house of Levi, bless you⌃ the Lord: you⌃ that fear the Lord, bless the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed in Sion be the Lord, who dwells in Jerusalem.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
